WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:04.940
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.340
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.180
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.320
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您带来终极的《办公室》粉丝播客。

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.820
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.020
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节以及许多闺蜜之间的故事。

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.040
We're the Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士 6.0》。

8
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:23.880
Hello.
你好。

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:27.580
Hi.
嗨。

10
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.220
Welcome back to Office Lady 6.0.
欢迎回到《办公室女士 6.0》。

11
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.300
Angela, are you ready for some jump scares?
安吉拉，你准备好迎接惊吓了吗？

12
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.960
Maybe some eerie music and a really scary villain?
也许还有些诡异的音乐和一个真正可怕的反派？

13
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.160
Why would I be ready for any of that?
我为什么要准备好迎接这些？

14
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.340
I don't know.
我不知道。

15
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.260
But you better get ready, because today we're breaking down the webisode, The Third Floor,
但你最好准备好，因为今天我们要解析网络剧集《三楼》，

16
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.760
which is all about Ryan making a horror movie.
讲的是瑞安拍恐怖电影的故事。

17
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.800
Well, Jenna, I know you're very excited for today's episode.
好吧，珍娜，我知道你对今天的剧集非常兴奋。

18
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.360
You love a good horror movie.
你很喜欢看恐怖片。

19
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:56.740
Love.
超爱。

20
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.040
I hate them.
我讨厌恐怖片。

21
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.300
But I want to tell you, I'm just thankful that there are no zombies in this one,
但我得告诉你，我很庆幸这一集里没有僵尸，

22
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.560
because I really hate zombies.
因为我真的很讨厌僵尸。

23
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.400
I love zombies.
我喜欢僵尸。

24
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.900
Give me all the zombies.
把所有僵尸都给我。

25
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.220
I mean, Ryan tried to have zombies.
我是说，瑞安确实尝试过加入僵尸。

26
00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:08.980
We'll get to it.
我们待会儿会讲到。

27
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:09.320
Yeah.
是啊。

28
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.060
I know.
我知道。

29
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:10.820
I got excited.
我当时很兴奋。

30
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.740
This is one thing you and I do have in common, though.
不过，这倒是你我之间的一个共同点。

31
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.660
What do we have in common?
我们有什么共同点？

32
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.920
Well, I don't know if we should talk about it, but we both had a really strong reaction
嗯，我不知道我们该不该提，但我们俩对

33
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.500
to the season of The Last of Us.
《最后生还者》那一季的反应都非常强烈。

34
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.260
You know, Josh had me watch it.
你知道，是乔什让我看的。

35
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.320
He wanted me to watch it.
他想让我看。

36
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.040
How did Josh get you to even start watching this?
乔什是怎么让你开始看这部剧的？

37
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.660
You watched the whole first season.
你可是看完了整整第一季。

38
00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:31.160
Yes.
是的。

39
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.300
And then you got hooked.
然后你就上瘾了。

40
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.220
I was very excited, because this is our first zombie crossover moment.
我当时很兴奋，因为这是我们第一次聊到僵尸题材。

41
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:36.800
Yeah.
是啊。

42
00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.420
I mean, I love Pedro.
我是说，我喜欢佩德罗。

43
00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:39.880
I love Pedro Pascal.
我喜欢佩德罗·帕斯卡。

44
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.940
Well, we all love Pedro Pascal, which is why this season was so very upsetting to us,
好吧，我们都喜欢佩德罗·帕斯卡，这就是为什么这一季让我们如此难过，

45
00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.560
because we didn't play the video game, everybody.
因为大家，我们没玩过那个电子游戏。

46
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.240
Jenna and I didn't know.
我和珍娜都不知道。

47
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.960
We didn't know what was going to happen.
我们不知道会发生什么。

48
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.740
And after it happened, I was so upset.
事情发生后，我难过极了。

49
00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:55.780
Jenna left me three.
珍娜给我留了三条语音。

50
00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:56.840
Okay.
好吧。

51
00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:01.920
If you don't know the video game, and if you haven't watched this show yet, just like—
如果你没玩过这款游戏，也没看过这部剧，那么——

52
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.720
Fast forward, maybe.
或许可以快进一下。

53
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.080
Fast forward, because I actually need to talk about this.
快进吧，因为我真的得聊聊这个。

54
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.340
And I know we're a little late to talking about it, because everyone expressed this same
我知道我们聊得有点晚了，因为大家在两个月前

55
00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.400
outrage about two months ago.
就已经表达过同样的愤慨了。

56
00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.480
But truly, if you haven't played the video game, and you haven't seen season two,
但说真的，如果你没玩过游戏，也没看过第二季，

57
00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.160
just fast forward about 50 seconds from now.
现在就直接快进50秒吧。

58
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:18.780
Yes.
没错。

59
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:26.240
Guys, Pedro Pascal's character has the most gruesome death in episode two.
伙计们，佩德罗·帕斯卡饰演的角色在第二集里死得太惨了。

60
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.820
In episode two.
就在第二集。

61
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.320
I kept waiting.
我一直等着。

62
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.540
I was like, wait, what?
我当时心想，等等，什么情况？

63
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.500
Shirley—oh, here she comes.
雪莉——哦，她来了。

64
00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.060
She's going to come rescue him.
她要去救他了。

65
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.000
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

66
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.900
And here's the thing.
关键是这样。

67
00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.700
I'm not watching it anymore.
我再也不看了。

68
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.400
I can't watch it anymore.
我实在看不下去了。

69
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:42.800
I like that.
我喜欢那个角色。

70
00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.920
He was my guy.
他可是我的心头好。

71
00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.500
You broke my heart.
你伤透了我的心。

72
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.660
Why would I keep going out with a guy who broke my heart like that?
我为什么要继续和一个伤透我心的男人交往呢？

73
00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:57.580
Like, the show is a man who I was in love with, and he f***ing trampled on my heart.
这部剧就像是一个我深爱的男人，他妈的把我的心给践踏了。

74
00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.700
I can't go back to him.
我没法再回到他身边了。

75
00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.700
I can't go back to him.
我没法再回到他身边了。

76
00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.060
It was too much for me.
这对我来说太沉重了。

77
00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.060
And I sent a text to our group thread where I was like, what?
我给我们的群组发了条信息，问这是怎么回事？

78
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.000
And I googled.
我还去谷歌搜了。

79
00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.460
I was like, what?
我当时想，什么鬼？

80
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.180
You gave me three, like, angry messages.
你给我发了三条特别愤怒的信息。

81
00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.480
Like, angry, long messages about what the hell just happened here.
就是那种愤怒的长篇大论，问这到底是怎么回事。

82
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.240
Yeah, we both were pretty bummed about that.
是啊，我们俩当时都挺难受的。

83
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.920
Josh is still watching, so he has continued without me.
乔什还在看，所以他没我陪着也继续看下去了。

84
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.540
I was like, I can't.
我当时说，我真的不行。

85
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.920
I was like, babe, here's the thing.
我说，宝贝，情况是这样的。

86
00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:32.020
You can't ask me, as someone who hates zombies.
你不能要求我，作为一个讨厌丧尸的人，

87
00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.260
I hate zombies.
我讨厌丧尸。

88
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:33.620
Yeah.
没错。

89
00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:39.180
You can't ask me to watch a zombie show with the one thing that kept me watching it.
你不能要求我继续看一部丧尸剧，而我坚持看下去的唯一动力，

90
00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:39.740
It's gone.
已经没了。

91
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:40.540
Yes.
是的。

92
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.680
That was the only reason I was there.
那是我看这部剧的唯一理由。

93
00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:43.280
Okay.
好吧。

94
00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.540
It wasn't the only reason I was there, but I am so distraught that I have not been able
那倒不是我看的唯一理由，但我实在太难过了，以至于

95
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.340
to keep watching it.
我根本没法继续看下去。

96
00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.260
I think I might.
我想我可能会吧。

97
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.760
I think I will get over this hurt.
我想我会从这次伤害中走出来的。

98
00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.140
But listen to me, everybody.
但听我说，各位。

99
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.160
We all know.
我们都懂的。

100
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.340
I was trying to explain it to Lee, because Lee doesn't watch it with me.
我当时试着跟李解释，因为李不跟我一起看。

101
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.200
He's like, I don't get, like, just this one person died.
他说，我不明白，怎么就死了一个人而已。

102
00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.200
I'm like, babe, babe, it's Pedro Pascal, okay?
我说，宝贝，宝贝，那可是佩德罗·帕斯卡，好吗？

103
00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.240
He is like, I tried to come up with, like, an analogy.
他说，我试着想出一个类比。

104
00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:16.840
I was like, he is, remember what Meg Ryan was to, like, an 80s romantic comedy movie?
我说，他就是，你还记得梅格·瑞恩对于80年代浪漫喜剧电影意味着什么吗？

105
00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:22.400
Just, like, an utter delight from the moment she's on screen until the end.
就是那种从她出现在银幕上那一刻起，直到电影结束，都让人感到无比愉悦的存在。

106
00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:22.740
Yeah.
没错。

107
00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.400
Like, just makes you happy watching her.
就是看着她就会让你感到开心。

108
00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.200
That is the feeling I get when I watch Pedro Pascal in anything.
这就是我看着佩德罗·帕斯卡出演任何作品时的感觉。

109
00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.060
Just a delight.
简直是一种享受。

110
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.660
I'm happier now.
我现在更开心了。

111
00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.680
You know what it is for me?
你知道对我来说这意味着什么吗？

112
00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:33.640
I'm invested.
我入戏了。

113
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.720
Whatever he's in, I'm so invested.
无论他演什么，我都深陷其中。

114
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.080
I still really, really need you to see his arc in Game of Thrones.
我还是非常、非常希望你能看看他在《权力的游戏》里的角色弧光。

115
00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.380
I really need you to get to Dorne.
我真的需要你看到多恩那个篇章。

116
00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.560
I am so sorry.
我很抱歉。

117
00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.560
I saw a red carpet interview with him where someone said,
我看到过一个他的红毯采访，有人问他，

118
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:55.960
will you ever have such a brutal death as you had in Game of Thrones that will upset fans?
你以后还会像在《权力的游戏》里那样死得那么惨，让粉丝们伤心吗？

119
00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:03.200
And he said, yes, I think there will be, because he knew what was going to happen in The Last of Us.
他说，会的，我想会的，因为他当时已经知道《最后生还者》里会发生什么了。

120
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.380
I still need you to see him in Game of Thrones.
我还是需要你去看看他在《权力的游戏》里的表现。

121
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:06.660
Sam.
萨姆。

122
00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.860
Yeah, I need you to watch that episode at leaSt.
对，我至少需要你去看看那一集。

123
00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.500
I don't want to just tune in to see him die.
我不想只为了看他死才去追剧。

124
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.800
You need to see the minute he comes on screen.
你需要看看他出现在银幕上的那一刻。

125
00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:22.000
His presence, it's so different from the other characters you've seen him play.
他的那种气场，和他之前演过的其他角色完全不同。

126
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.100
I need you, I need you to see him.
我需要你，我需要你去看看他。

127
00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.360
My introduction to him was in Game of Thrones.
我最初认识他是在《权力的游戏》里。

128
00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.200
Okay, my introduction to him was in Narcos.
好吧，我最初认识他是在《毒枭》里。

129
00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.380
Oh, he's great in Narcos.
噢，他在《毒枭》里演得太棒了。

130
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.100
Okay, I will watch Game of Thrones for Pedro Pascal.
好吧，为了佩德罗·帕斯卡，我会去看《权力的游戏》的。

131
00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:35.700
Like, done.
就这么定了。

132
00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:36.460
I will do it.
我会去看的。

133
00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.400
What season is he?
他是第几季出现的？

134
00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.580
Like, how far in?
大概要看多久？

135
00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:42.480
I mean, could she just pick up with that season, Sam?
我是说，她可以直接从那一季开始看吗，萨姆？

136
00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.380
She doesn't have to, like, watch all the way to when they have the Dorne brother sisters on.
她不需要非得一直看到多恩那些姐妹们出场吧。

137
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.620
So he first appears in season four, episode one.
他是在第四季第一集首次登场的。

138
00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:53.220
Oh, my God.
天哪。

139
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:53.840
Thank you, Cassie.
谢谢你，卡西。

140
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:54.240
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

141
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.500
I say just go there.
我说就直接看那一季吧。

142
00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.100
Don't.
别。

143
00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:00.760
I got pretty far into Game of Thrones when I committed to watching it.
我当初下定决心看《权力的游戏》时，已经看了挺长一段了。

144
00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:07.740
Like, I'm pretty sure, I've told you, like, when is that red lady on that extra island?
我记得我跟你说过，就是那个在额外岛屿上的红袍女是什么时候出现的？

145
00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.160
The red wedding?
你是说红色婚礼吗？

146
00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:08.740
Yeah.
对。

147
00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:10.820
Isn't that, like, in season three or something?
那不是在第三季左右吗？

148
00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:11.480
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

149
00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.320
You're not talking about the red wedding.
你说的不是红色婚礼。

150
00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.200
You're talking about the red lady who had sex with the black smoke.
你指的是那个和黑烟发生关系的红袍女。

151
00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:16.880
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

152
00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:17.560
Yeah, her.
对，就是她。

153
00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.240
Yeah.
嗯。

154
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.040
I don't know what season that is, but that was around where it lost me.
我不知道那是第几季，但大概就是在那儿我看不下去了。

155
00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.420
I would pick up, I would start season three.
我会从第三季开始看。

156
00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:29.760
I would watch season three and then treat yourself with a first episode of season four at the end.
我会看完第三季，最后再看一集第四季的第一集犒劳一下自己。

157
00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.880
Have you seen the red wedding episode?
你看过“血色婚礼”那一集吗？

158
00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.720
I don't know what happens in a red wedding.
我不知道血色婚礼里发生了什么。

159
00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.160
Oh, you would know.
哦，你肯定会知道的。

160
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:34.740
Never mind.
算了。

161
00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:35.240
Never mind.
算了。

162
00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.840
That's a great episode.
那集非常精彩。

163
00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:37.500
Okay.
好吧。

164
00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:38.020
Okay.
好的。

165
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.260
Well, we might have to make a list for her.
好吧，我们可能得给她列个清单。

166
00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:41.900
Well, you know what?
嗯，你知道吗？

167
00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.320
We should probably take a break because when we come back, we are going to break down the third floor.
我们大概该休息一下了，因为回来之后，我们要剖析一下三楼。

168
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:52.160
And Jenna, as our resident horror movie expert, you're going to give us your assessment of Ryan's attempt at this genre.
珍娜，作为我们的常驻恐怖片专家，你要给我们评价一下瑞安对这个类型的尝试。

169
00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:52.840
I will.
我会的。

170
00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:53.520
I will.
我会的。

171
00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.900
I tried to give it my best critique.
我试着给出了我最好的评价。

172
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:56.420
Okay.
好的。

173
00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.680
But that's not all, everybody.
但还没完，各位。

174
00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.540
I gave Angela an assignment.
我给安吉拉布置了一个任务。

175
00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:00.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

176
00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.460
That I'm so excited about.
我对此感到非常兴奋。

177
00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:07.560
I asked her to watch the first 24 minutes and 30 seconds of John Carpenter's The Thing.
我让她看了约翰·卡朋特执导的《怪形》的前24分30秒。

178
00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:07.960
Yep.
没错。

179
00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:14.040
Because that is about the same amount of time that I watched the first John Wick movie on my first viewing.
因为那和我第一次看第一部《疾速追杀》时看的时间长度差不多。

180
00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.780
I have completed it, everyone.
大家都看完了。

181
00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.220
But Angela said she would watch that same length of any horror movie I chose.
但安吉拉说她愿意看我选的任何恐怖片，只要时长一样就行。

182
00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.140
And I did.
我确实看了。

183
00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.080
And I have no idea what her reaction is.
我完全不知道她的反应会是什么。

184
00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:23.800
Don't tell me yet.
先别告诉我。

185
00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.760
But I cannot wait to hear your thoughts.
但我迫不及待想听听你的想法了。

186
00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:35.300
And Angela, I want you to know that I tried really hard to pick a movie that was not just a horror movie, but also a classically great film.
安吉拉，我想让你知道，我真的很努力地选了一部电影，它不仅是恐怖片，也是一部经典的伟大电影。

187
00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.100
I didn't just try to, like, give you some slasher scary thing.
我不是只想随便给你找个吓人的砍杀片。

188
00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:39.820
That's true.
确实如此。

189
00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:40.960
And I appreciate that.
我很感激这一点。

190
00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.360
I truly knew nothing about this movie before I watched it.
在看这部电影之前，我真的对它一无所知。

191
00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.320
I did not Google it.
我没有去谷歌搜索。

192
00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.220
I did not look it up.
我没有去查资料。

193
00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.180
I really watched it not knowing anything.
我真的是在什么都不知道的情况下看的。

194
00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:51.640
So it was just my honest reaction as I started watching it.
所以这完全是我刚开始看时的真实反应。

195
00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.920
And I will share that with you.
我会和你们分享的。

196
00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:53.700
All right.
好吧。

197
00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.360
Well, we'll take a break.
那我们先休息一下。

198
00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:56.140
Be right back.
马上回来。

199
00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.840
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老成员。

200
00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:09.720
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是《我们不在乎俱乐部》播客。

201
00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.900
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们步入中年，意识到自己真的没那么在乎了。

202
00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:22.000
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理解潮热、耳朵痒、下巴长毛、琐碎的家庭、脑雾和蝴蝶袖这些事。

203
00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.860
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听见。

204
00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.780
So come join the WDNC.
所以，加入“我们不在乎俱乐部”（WDNC）吧。

205
00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:32.320
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在各大播客平台关注并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的《我们不在乎俱乐部》播客。

206
00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.440
All right.
好的。

207
00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.680
We are back.
我们回来了。

208
00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.640
And this webisode series has some really fun bonus content on Peacock.
这个网络剧集系列在孔雀视频（Peacock）上有一些非常有趣的额外内容。

209
00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:50.360
Like, there is this cool black and white film slipbook of behind the scenes of this shoot.
比如，有一本很酷的黑白幕后花絮翻页书，记录了这次拍摄的过程。

210
00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.020
It was really fun to watch.
看的时候真的很有趣。

211
00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:53.540
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

212
00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.440
There's also some interviews with the caSt.
还有一些演员访谈。

213
00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:01.080
I thought we should kick this off with what Mindy and BJ had to say about this webisode series.
我想我们应该先从敏迪和BJ对这个网络剧集的评价开始。

214
00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:06.860
The episodes are following the tradition of the characters wanting to put on a show.
这些剧集延续了角色们想要表演节目的传统。

215
00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:14.320
Ryan is directing a horror film that he thinks will be sort of the paranormal activity set in an office.
瑞安正在导演一部恐怖片，他认为这会是那种以办公室为背景的《灵动：鬼影实录》式的电影。

216
00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:19.020
Picked up by the documentary crew and by the main characters in the office.
由纪录片摄制组和办公室里的主角们拍摄。

217
00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.420
Like, the little things that fall through the cracks.
就像那些容易被忽略的小事。

218
00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.400
I think that's the best thing to show in a webisode.
我觉得这是网络剧集最适合展现的内容。

219
00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:28.440
So I really liked when the group did Subtle Sexuality, that girl band that Kelly and Erin did.
我真的很喜欢之前那个组合做的“微妙性感”（Subtle Sexuality），就是凯莉和艾琳组成的那个女子乐队。

220
00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.400
And I really liked this horror film that they're all working on.
我也很喜欢他们现在正在制作的这部恐怖片。

221
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.420
It's funny, like, the side projects that just get completely ignored by everyone in the office.
很有趣，就像那些在办公室里完全被大家忽视的副业项目。

222
00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.440
And somehow, for the webisodes, we capture them.
而不知何故，我们在网络剧集里捕捉到了它们。

223
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.080
I like that.
我喜欢这一点。

224
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:41.660
I do, too.
我也是。

225
00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:45.780
So it's really fun that they get to explore what Ryan's passions or hobbies are.
所以能探索瑞安的爱好或热情所在，真的很有趣。

226
00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.700
And I guess he's a big horror film fan.
我猜他是个恐怖片大影迷。

227
00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.740
Well, I think it's more that he's a filmmaking fan.
嗯，我觉得与其说是影迷，不如说他是个电影制作迷。

228
00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:56.960
And this, to me, kind of goes with his character trait of, like, how he got into photography for a while.
对我来说，这和他的人物性格很契合，就像他之前有一阵子迷上摄影一样。

229
00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:02.700
I feel like the horror movie part is just his way into being a, like, film director.
我觉得拍恐怖片只是他成为电影导演的一种途径。

230
00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.140
Oh, yes, and entertainment.
哦，是的，还有娱乐性。

231
00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.080
Well, there's more cast interviews.
好了，还有更多的演员访谈。

232
00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.580
We'll sprinkle those in as we go.
我们会在节目进行过程中穿插播放。

233
00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:11.040
Well, here are a few stats about this webisode.
那么，这里有一些关于这个网络剧集的数据。

234
00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.340
It was released on October 28, 2010.
它发布于2010年10月28日。

235
00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:17.200
This was during Season 7 of The Office.
当时正值《办公室》第七季期间。

236
00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:22.020
We aired the episode costume contest the same day as this webisode.
我们在播出这一网络剧集的同一天，播出了剧集《服装竞赛》。

237
00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.020
It was kind of our nod to Halloween.
这算是我们对万圣节的致敬。

238
00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:29.000
This webisode was also nominated for a Webby Award.
这个网络剧集还获得了威比奖提名。

239
00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.540
So episode one is titled Kelly and Erin Move On.
第一集的标题是《凯莉和艾琳向前看》。

240
00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:38.980
This whole series of webisodes were written by Kelly Hannon, Jonathan Hughes, and Mary Wall.
这一整个系列的网络剧集是由凯莉·汉农、乔纳森·休斯和玛丽·沃尔编写的。

241
00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.440
And they were directed by Mindy Kaling.
并由敏迪·卡灵执导。

242
00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:43.260
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

243
00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:48.200
Kelly and Erin are going to pivot away from subtle sexuality.
凯莉和艾琳打算从“微妙性感”转型。

244
00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.720
They're not going to make music anymore.
她们不再做音乐了。

245
00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:56.240
Their new creative outlet is going to be acting in Ryan's horror film.
她们新的创意出口将是出演瑞安的恐怖片。

246
00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:57.080
Yeah.
没错。

247
00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:01.140
As the series starts, we are at front reception.
剧集开始时，我们在前台。

248
00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:05.480
Kelly and Erin are listening to the tail end of their song, I'm Just the Girl Next Door.
凯莉和艾琳正在听她们歌曲《我只是邻家女孩》的结尾部分。

249
00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.780
Erin thinks it's their best one yet.
艾琳认为这是她们迄今为止最好的一首歌。

250
00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:11.700
But they are disappointed by how many views the video is getting.
但她们对视频的观看量感到失望。

251
00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:12.760
It's not getting very many.
没几个人看。

252
00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:13.420
Two.
两个。

253
00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:14.140
Two.
两个。

254
00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.300
That's it.
就这些。

255
00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.880
Dare I say it's the two of them watching it?
我敢说是因为他们两个在看吗？

256
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:19.220
I think so.
我想是吧。

257
00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.940
Kelly declares that music and dance are dead.
凯莉宣称音乐和舞蹈已经死了。

258
00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:22.960
That's it.
就是这样。

259
00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:23.880
That must be the reason.
那一定是原因所在。

260
00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.540
Yes, that's why.
没错，就是因为这个。

261
00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.660
Erin does add it's also the economy.
艾琳补充说还有经济原因。

262
00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.060
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

263
00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.640
So there are multiple reasons.
所以原因不止一个。

264
00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.240
They say maybe it's time to move on.
她们说也许是时候向前看了。

265
00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.560
But don't worry.
但别担心。

266
00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:35.900
They're not giving up on fame.
她们并没有放弃成名。

267
00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.600
They're just giving up on music.
她们只是放弃了音乐。

268
00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.560
So we cut to a little sitting area outside the break room.
镜头切到休息室外的一个小休息区。

269
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.660
Kelly and Erin are now with Kevin.
凯莉和艾琳现在正和凯文在一起。

270
00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.380
They are sitting on the floor.
她们坐在地板上。

271
00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.940
They're having a floor chat.
她们在进行地板谈话。

272
00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.140
Yes, like a little brainstorming session.
是的，就像一场小型的头脑风暴会议。

273
00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.460
I've never seen this staging before.
我以前从没见过这种场景布置。

274
00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.880
I found it super creative and interesting and fun.
我觉得这非常有创意、有趣且好玩。

275
00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:55.500
Fun.
好玩。

276
00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:56.480
Yeah, I loved it.
是啊，我很喜欢。

277
00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:01.240
It kind of reminded me a little bit about when there was that group in the little supply
这让我想起之前那个小组在小储藏室里开会的时候，

278
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.220
closet having a meeting, like Kelly and Toby.
比如凯莉和托比。

279
00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:09.540
Yes, that was added back to the super fan episode of, what was that?
对，那是加回超级粉丝版剧集里的，那是哪一集来着？

280
00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.140
Hot Girl.
《辣妹》。

281
00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.140
Yes.
对。

282
00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:15.420
It was a really, really creative way to shoot this.
这是一种非常、非常有创意的拍摄方式。

283
00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:21.240
Kelly has like a little pad of paper, I guess, for her brainstorming session.
凯莉好像有个小记事本，我想是用来做头脑风暴的。

284
00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.920
I need you to hear how Kelly kicks things off.
你需要听听凯莉是怎么开场的。

285
00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:26.060
Okay.
好的。

286
00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:30.780
I want to express myself, but I have nothing to say and no medium with which to do it.
我想表达自己，但我没什么可说的，也没有表达的媒介。

287
00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:32.040
That's it.
就是这样。

288
00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.240
She has something she wants to say.
她有想说的话。

289
00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.960
She doesn't know what it is.
她不知道那是什么。

290
00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.380
She has no way to do it.
她没有表达的方式。

291
00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:37.620
Right.
没错。

292
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:37.820
Go.
开始吧。

293
00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:45.520
Well, Kevin explains that there's more than one way to express yourself, and he reveals
嗯，凯文解释说表达自己的方式不止一种，他还透露

294
00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.060
that he writes poetry.
他会写诗。

295
00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.160
What?
什么？

296
00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:51.280
All along, Kevin is a poet?
原来凯文一直是个诗人？

297
00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.500
He reads one of his haikus.
他读了他的一首俳句。

298
00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:54.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

299
00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.540
Here's what it is.
内容是这样的。

300
00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.480
Beauty approaches.
美，悄然而至。

301
00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.080
I am brought under its spell.
我被它深深吸引了。

302
00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.180
I long to be with.
我渴望与它在一起。

303
00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:04.380
That's it.
就是这样。

304
00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:05.900
Because he ran out of syllables.
因为他音节用完了。

305
00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:06.320
That's it.
就是这样。

306
00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.140
We'll never know.
我们永远不会知道。

307
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.320
Ryan is in the adjacent room, and he is yelling at someone over the phone.
瑞安在隔壁房间，正对着电话大吼大叫。

308
00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:13.460
He's very upset.
他非常生气。

309
00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:14.380
Yes.
是的。

310
00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:20.860
He's talking about, like, ancient zombies traipsing through Scranton out for blood.
他好像在说古代僵尸在斯克兰顿街头游荡，到处寻仇。

311
00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:26.440
Instead, Ryan is on the phone with someone trying to get them to participate.
相反，瑞安正在电话里试图说服某人参与其中。

312
00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:27.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

313
00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:28.540
It sounds like he needs—
听起来他需要——

314
00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:28.940
Would you say?
你会怎么说？

315
00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:29.420
Yes.
是的。

316
00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:32.440
It sounds like he needs a lot of background actors to play zombies.
听起来他需要很多背景演员来扮演僵尸。

317
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.060
Yes.
是的。

318
00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:36.860
And we find out that he is called the evergreen old folks home.
然后我们发现他打给了常青养老院。

319
00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:37.680
Yes.
是的。

320
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.580
